    "description": "Salesforce Solution Architect A government contract requires that this position be restricted to U.S. citizens. You must provide documentation that you are a U.S. citizen. Public Trust eligible. Position Summary: We’re seeking a highly motivated Salesforce Solution Architect to join our team supporting a Salesforce initiative. As a Salesforce Solution Architect, you will play a critical role in designing, developing, and articulating solutions based on our customers' strategic business and technical requirements. You will collaborate with various stakeholders, including program managers, technical peers, and business partners, to ensure the delivery of maximum value to our clients. You will lead the implementation effort, taking responsibility for delivering architecture designs and solution strategies. Strong communication, analytical, and time management skills are essential, as well as a continual willingness to learn new technologies in a fast-paced environment.Problem-solving capabilities must be excellent, and you should possess a resilient, flexible, and enthusiastic personality. Compensation &amp; Benefits: Starting Salary Range for Salesforce Solution Architect: $175,00-195,000 Benefits That Set Us Apart When considering your next opportunity, compensation is only part of the picture. We offer a benefits package designed to invest in your future and support your life outside of work. Highlights include: Up to a 6% 401(k) company match to help you build long-term financial security Paid time off as part of our comprehensive benefits package, so you have the flexibility to rest, recharge, and enjoy what matters most Medical, dental, and vision insurance, plus prescription drug coverage Basic life and AD&amp;D insurance, with supplemental life options Short-term and long-term disability coverage •Paid holidays •Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Flexible Spending Account (FSA) and Health Savings Account (HSA) options Professional development, training, and certification support Voluntary benefits including accident, critical illness, and identity theft protection Because taking care of our employees isn’t just a promise, it’s part of who we are. Benefits are subject to change and eligibility requirements apply. Essential Functions, Duties &amp; Responsibilities: Includes the following: Experience in providing program oversight and solutions architecture for Salesforce applications. Excellent verbal and written communication skills for technical and non-technical audiences, as well as senior management. •Strong relationship management skills. Experience in Salesforce with end-to-end implementation in the following areas: Solution Architect experience on implementation projects using Agile and Iterative approaches. Understanding of key SFDC architectural concepts and their influence on design. Experience deploying solutions that include Experience Cloud. Evaluation of Salesforce with 3rd party solutions. Background in architecture concepts (integration styles, architecture styles, patterns). Strong knowledge of software quality assurance best practices and methodologies. Knowledge of Business Process Management (BPM) techniques and tools. •Must be a US Citizen. Must pass pre-employment qualifications of Cherokee Federal . Perform other job-related duties as assigned. Basic Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, or a related field. A Master's degree is preferred. Will have a minimum of five (5) years of general work experience. Experience in the IT field focusing on Salesforce and/or other no-code/low-code platform projects, DevSecOps, and technical architecture. Will possess strong architecture and design experience, including at least three (3) years of experience architecting Salesforce production enterprise applications. •US. Citizenship is required Prolonged periods of sitting at a desk and working on a computer; may occasionally require standing or moving about the office for extended periods. Must pass pre-employment qualifications of Cherokee Federal . Preferred Qualifications: Salesforce Certifications (Sales Cloud/Service Cloud Consultant, Experience Cloud Consultant) preferred. Company Information: Behind every government mission stands skilled, mission-driven talent: people whose expertise and dedication turn complex challenges into successful outcomes. HESFP, LLC, part of Cherokee Federal , the federal contracting division of Cherokee Nation Businesses, is that team. We modernize aging systems, deliver care where it’s needed most, and keep missions supplied, staffed, and moving across defense, intelligence, and civilian agencies. For more than 60 federal clients, we take on the work others won’t, and deliver where it counts. If that’s the kind of work you’re looking for, you’ve found your team. Learn more at cherokee-federal.com. #CherokeeFederal Cherokee Federal is a military friendly employer. Veterans and active military transitioning to civilian status are encouraged to apply. Legal Disclaimer: All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to protected veteran status, disability or any other status protected under applicable federal, state or local law. Many of our job openings require access to government buildings or military installations. Candidates must pass pre-employment qualifications of Cherokee Federal . For applicants located in Colorado, New York, California, Washington, Illinois, Hawaii, Massachusetts, or other states with pay transparency requirements: the estimated annual salary range for this position is available upon request. Actual compensation varies based on qualifications, experience, and location. Equal Employment Opportunity (EEO) Statement Cherokee Federal is a federal contractor subject to the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act (VEVRAA). As required by VEVRAA, we take affirmative action to employ and advance in employment qualified protected veterans. Protected veterans are encouraged to self-identify during the application process. Cherokee Federal takes affirmative action to employ and advance in employment qualified individuals with disabilities in compliance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act. Qualified individuals with disabilities are encouraged to self-identify during the application process. Reasonable accommodations are available to qualified individuals with disabilities or those with sincerely held religious beliefs. To request an accommodation in the application or interview process, please contact Human Resources at . This position is subject to pre-employment drug testing. Cherokee Federal maintains a drug-free workplace in accordance with applicable federal and state laws and regulations. This position may be contingent upon the successful completion of a background investigation. The scope of the investigation will be commensurate with position requirements and applicable law. Originally posted on Himalayas",
