    "title": "Regional Brand Protection Analyst - Data Labeling & Enforcement (Arabic Speaker)",
    "company_name": "Corsearch",
    "company_logo": "https://cdn-images.himalayas.app/4um3dvgrz8wjs62pbt7sozorpg4v",
    "description": "At Corsearch , we are dedicated to creating a world where consumers can trust the choices they make. As a global leader in Trademark and Brand Protection, we partner with businesses to safeguard their most valuable assets in an increasingly complex digital environment. Our comprehensive solutions, powered by AI-driven data and deep analytics, enable brands to establish, monitor, and protect their presence against infringement and counterfeiting. Why Choose Corsearch ? Innovative Solutions : We combine cutting-edge technology with expert judgment to deliver market-leading services in trademark clearance, brand protection, and anti-counterfeiting. Global Impact : Trusted by over 5,000 customers worldwide, including 73 of Fortune's Top 100 companies, our work has a meaningful impact on businesses and consumers alike. Collaborative Culture : With a team of over 1,900 professionals across multiple global offices, you'll be joining an inclusive environment where diverse perspectives thrive. Mission-Driven Purpose : Our commitment to protecting consumers and their trust in brands drives everything we do, making Corsearch a force for good in the world. ✅The Role Corsearch is seeking a Brand Protection Analyst to join a team dedicated to one of the world's leading consumer health and hygiene companies. This analyst will specialize in the UAE and broader Middle East markets, bringing the specific language skills (Arabic) and local marketplace expertise needed to identify infringing activity that standard monitoring may miss. ✅Responsibilities and Duties Proactive Brand Protection Identify, moderate, and enforce counterfeit, lookalike, and other potentially infringing activity affecting the client's brands across the UAE and the Middle East. Research sellers, connected accounts, and repeat offenders, recognizing emerging threats and infringement patterns, and establishing which targets deserve priority. Actively look for enforcement opportunities beyond existing monitoring results and own the end-to-end process of identification, quality assurance, and enforcement of infringing content. Conduct proactive online local-language research beyond Zeal, identifying and mapping significant sellers, connected accounts, and repeat offenders. Local Marketplace Expertise Demonstrate strong familiarity with the leading e-commerce platforms in the Middle East and their country-specific sites. Understand each platform's requirements, seller behavior, and enforcement processes. Navigate regional access requirements seamlessly. Identify market-specific challenges and opportunities that could improve the client's brand protection coverage. Regional Language and Market Knowledge Working in Arabic at a professional level, you will understand local terminology, consumer behavior, and regional e-commerce practices. Apply this knowledge to uncover infringing activity that may not surface through standard monitoring. Identify emerging local platforms, channels, seller behaviors, and market-specific threats and trends. Provide concise regional intelligence on what is changing, where the risks are, and where we should focus. Support country-specific research and enforcement requirements. Intelligence-Led Brand Protection Use Corsearch 's Zeal platform alongside your own local marketplace research to find actionable infringement opportunities. Prioritize targets based on risk, scale, and potential impact rather than simply relying on volume. Collaboration and Reporting Work closely with the dedicated Corsearch account team, including the Brand Protection Partners, analysts, and operational management. Highlight significant sellers, emerging infringement trends, and regional platform challenges. Provide local market insight to inform enforcement strategy and prioritization. Communicate your findings, progress, and recommendations clearly to the relevant stakeholders. ✅Essential Professional proficiency in Arabic and fluent English. Strong knowledge of the Middle East's main e-commerce platforms. Experience in online brand protection, intellectual property enforcement, marketplace monitoring, or a related field. Solid understanding of counterfeit products, lookalike products, and other forms of online intellectual property infringement. Comfortable conducting detailed online research and analyzing seller behavior. Familiarity with brand protection platforms and analytical tools. Strong analytical, problem-solving, and communication skills. Strong data management and interpretation skills. Ability to work independently, proactively identify opportunities, and collaborate effectively with both regional and global teams. Corsearch is an equal opportunity and inclusive employer and does not tolerate discrimination of any kind. We are committed to creating a diverse and inclusive workplace where all employees feel valued, respected, and supported. We welcome applications from all individuals regardless of race, nationality, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, age, disability, or any other protected characteristic. Together, we are working proactively to build a workplace where everyone can belong and be at their best selves. Together, we make an Impact. Originally posted on Himalayas",
