    "title": "Clinical Data Management Associate II",
    "company_name": "Clario",
    "company_logo": "https://cdn-images.himalayas.app/df00e5vwoiy66nlfr8guvq7sytxr",
    "description": "Join Clario , a part of Thermo Fisher Scientific and help ensure the quality, accuracy, and integrity of clinical trial data that supports the development of life-changing therapies worldwide. As a Clinical Data Management Associate II within our Medical Imaging business, you will play an important role in reviewing, validating, and managing clinical trial data generated from imaging studies across multiple therapeutic areas. Working closely with project teams, sponsors, and operational stakeholders, you will help drive data quality, support study execution, and contribute to the delivery of reliable clinical data that enables critical research decisions. What We Offer Competitive pay and incentives. Provident fund and medical insurance. Engaging employee programs and local events. Modern office spaces and remote work flexibility. Opportunities for professional growth and career development within a global organization. What You'll Be Doing Review study documentation and project requirements to assess impacts on Clinical Data Management processes, standards, and deliverables. Collaborate with cross-functional teams to support study setup, data collection strategies, and evolving project requirements. Support the implementation and execution of data management plans for assigned imaging studies. Define, execute, review, and maintain edit checks to identify discrepancies and ensure high-quality clinical data. Review clinical and imaging-related data to identify inconsistencies, trends, and data quality issues. Develop and maintain study data specifications, including data transfer specifications, system configuration specifications, and data validation requirements. Create, review, and maintain transmittal forms and study documentation while ensuring compliance with established standards. Collaborate with project teams to investigate and resolve data discrepancies and outstanding issues. Track data-related issues through resolution and ensure timely follow-up with relevant stakeholders. Prepare, validate, and deliver ad hoc data listings and study reports as required. Identify system enhancements, bugs, or process improvement opportunities and coordinate communication with appropriate Product Management teams. Maintain complete, accurate, and audit-ready study documentation throughout the study lifecycle. Communicate project status, risks, and data quality concerns to supervisors and project stakeholders. Contribute to departmental process improvement initiatives, SOP updates, and quality enhancement activities. Support compliance with company procedures, Good Clinical Practice requirements, and applicable regulatory expectations. What We Look For Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Life Sciences, Healthcare, Clinical Research, Data Science, or a related field preferred, or equivalent professional experience. Minimum 3 or 3+ years of experience in Clinical Data Management, clinical research, biotechnology, pharmaceutical, CRO, or related healthcare environments. Understanding of clinical trial processes, data review methodologies, and clinical database management principles. Working knowledge of relational database concepts, data validation techniques, and quality control processes. Experience developing or maintaining data specifications, edit checks, data transfer requirements, or study configuration documentation preferred. Familiarity with clinical trial terminology and regulated research environments. Proficiency with Microsoft Office applications, including Word, Excel, Access, Outlook, and PowerPoint. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to identify and resolve data quality issues. Excellent attention to detail and commitment to data accuracy and quality. Strong organizational, documentation, and time-management skills. Excellent verbal and written communication skills with the ability to communicate effectively in English. Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively within cross-functional and global teams. Professional, proactive, and customer-focused approach with a commitment to continuous improvement. At Clario , a part of Thermo Fisher Scientific, our purpose is to transform lives by unlocking better evidence. It’s a cause that unites and inspires us. It’s why we come to work and how we empower our people to make a positive impact every day. Whether you're advancing clinical science, building innovative technology, or supporting our global teams, your work helps bring life-changing therapies to patients faster. Originally posted on Himalayas",
