    "title": "Management Consultant - Manager/Senior Manager - Munich",
    "company_name": "Efficioconsulting",
    "company_logo": null,
    "description": "Efficio is the world's largest specialist procurement and supply chain consultancy. Headquartered in London, we have offices across Europe, the Americas, East Asia, and the Middle East. We're a diverse team of more than 1,300 people, representing 60+ nationalities and speaking 40+ languages – and we're still growing! &nbsp; What sets us apart? We’re committed to delivering sustainable, measurable value for our clients. Our specialist focus means you'll develop deep expertise, while our hands-on approach to partnering with clients from strategy to implementation means you'll see the impact of your work. You'll have the opportunity to work on projects around the world in a wide variety of sectors, collaborating with colleagues from across our global offices. &nbsp; We are currently recruiting new team members across Germany, where you'll join a growing team of 50+ people.&nbsp;Our consultants work on a range of engagements, from rapid assessments to short-term savings programmes to long-term partnerships to help clients achieve lasting value. &nbsp; Consultants based in Germany work with clients across the country and Europe, with opportunities to take on projects beyond Europe as well.&nbsp; Your responsibilities: Leading consulting engagements from initial analysis and strategy development through to implementation and delivery. Identifying opportunities for cost optimisation, procurement transformation and supply chain improvement. Managing project teams, ensuring high-quality deliverables, effective collaboration and successful project outcomes. Building trusted relationships with senior client stakeholders, understanding their business priorities and translating these into actionable solutions. Supporting the development and mentoring of consultants, helping them grow professionally and deliver strong results. Contributing to business development activities, including identifying new opportunities and supporting client proposals. For Senior Manager positions, there will be an increased emphasis on managing complex engagements, developing client relationships and contributing to the growth of our business. What you'll bring: We're interested in experienced professionals who enjoy solving complex business challenges, building strong client relationships and delivering tangible results.&nbsp; &nbsp; Fluency in both German and English. Previous management consulting experience, with strong expertise in Strategic sourcing, procurement transformation or supply chain management. Experience managing projects and leading teams, including responsibility for project delivery and client relationships. Strong analytical, problem-solving and communication skills. Experience working with senior stakeholders and navigating complex business environments. A strong academic background. Previous business development experience would be particularly valuable, especially for Senior Manager positions. Location & Work Arrangements We welcome applications from candidates based across Germany. &nbsp; While Efficio's German office is located in Düsseldorf, you'll be part of our wider Germany consulting team, collaborating with colleagues locally and across our international offices. &nbsp; Our hybrid working model combines flexibility with regular in-person collaboration. We expect colleagues to spend approximately 10 working days per month in person, either at our Düsseldorf office or at client sites, depending on project requirements. &nbsp; Outside of these commitments, you'll have the flexibility to work remotely from your home location, subject to client and project needs. Why Join Efficio? At Efficio, we offer the opportunity to develop your expertise, make a tangible impact and grow as part of a truly global team. &nbsp; Deep Expertise: Work alongside experienced specialists, deepen your knowledge of procurement and supply chain, and continue developing your skills through challenging projects, mentorship and career development opportunities. &nbsp; Real World Impact: Go beyond recommendations and take ownership of delivering meaningful change. From strategy through implementation, you'll work closely with clients to solve complex challenges and achieve measurable, lasting results. &nbsp; One Global Team: Be part of a collaborative and international environment where diverse perspectives are valued. Work with colleagues across different countries, industries and backgrounds, sharing knowledge and learning from one another. &nbsp; If you're looking to deepen your expertise, make a real difference for clients and grow your career within a global team, we'd love to hear from you. Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow",
