    "title": "Operations Expert with Python for AI Supply Chain Task Design",
    "company_name": "Toptal",
    "company_logo": "",
    "description": "Overview A fast-growing AI data company is hiring supply chain practitioners to design expert-level Terminal-Bench tasks for evaluating AI agents. You will turn real planning work into end-to-end challenges, each with files, a working solution and an automated correctness check. The goal is to build a benchmark grounded in real operations work. ***THIS IS A TASK BASED COMPENSATION MODEL. PLEASE CHECK THE APPLICATION QUESTIONS FOR MORE DETAILS.*** Responsibilities â¢ Design expert-level Terminal-Bench tasks by turning a real supply chain task from your work into a challenge an AI agent solves end to end. â¢ Define the files, data exports and systems each task runs on, such as ERP, MES and WMS extracts, so the scenario reflects realistic planning conditions. â¢ Write a working solution for each task, for example a 5-day production plan, and confirm it can be solved in 60 to 75 minutes. â¢ Build the automated check that proves the result is correct, using tests or scripts that accept valid answers and catch planning errors objectively. â¢ Document the written rules, constraints and SOPs that decide each case, along with realistic edge cases, data inconsistencies and common planner errors from your process. â¢ Iterate on tasks based on reviewer feedback, keeping instructions unambiguous, data consistent and the solution and verification reproducible in a command-line environment. Skills/Experience â¢ 3+ years of hands-on supply chain or production planning work (not only studying, selling or managing it), or a PhD with active research in the subfield â¢ Did the work within the last 3 years and can name the systems, tools, data and rules used â¢ Personally executed a process where each case is decided by written rules such as SOPs, planning rules or constraints â¢ Worked inside systems of record (ERP, WMS) and with their exports or reports â¢ Can describe edge cases, data inconsistencies and common planner errors, and how a mistake would be caught â¢ Technical fluency in Python or another language and the command line, plus files, CSV/JSON, APIs or databases â¢ Available to start around November 4, 2026 Nice-to-have â¢ Automated or audited the process with scripts, SQL, RPA or rules engines â¢ 5+ years in the same process family â¢ Docker, Git and experience writing tests â¢ Hands-on experience with SAP or other ERPs and TMS/WMS platforms â¢ Advanced Excel skills Process â¢ Task-based engagement paid per task, with each task taking about 60 to 75 minutes â¢ Vetting task instead of a live interview â¢ Tasks are reviewed by the client before approval Please mention the word **EXELLENT** and tag RNDcuMTEuMy44OQ== when applying to show you read the job post completely (#RNDcuMTEuMy44OQ==). This is a beta feature to avoid spam applicants. Companies can search these words to find applicants that read this and see they're human.",
